            "review_text": "P12333165\nTemecula, California33 contributions\n1\nCan't Send Me Away\nOct 2017 • Solo\nI found this restaurant online and read it's known for it's duck hotpot so when I got here I told them I want duck hotpot in English and they definitely did not understand me. The one person who had small understanding of English indicated to me that I was at the wrong spot, what I was looking for was far down the road and I need a taxi to get there. But I buckled down, indicated I was already seated and going to eat there LOL. So they shrugged and gave me a menu, showed me the photo of the duck hotpot and I nodded away and away we went. The duck hotpot was delicious and I received half a duck, which was a lot for me but I ate as much as I could. Overall I got a beer and hotpot and it was a little over $6! I spent over $30 in Taipei for sucky overrated porridge hotpot and felt redeemed with this meal :) So if you come here just indicate you want a menu and order, don't try to say you want \"duck hotpot\".\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 7, 2017",
